{"archetypes":[{"name":"loop-state-ordering","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Verifies the pseudocode guard ordering is unambiguous across every documented edge case — broken-panel before zero-findings, main-agent-vote before revise, DEGRADED_PANEL before convergence streak.","prompt_body":"The plan's outer loop pseudocode specifies a strict ordering of guards: `_paths_readable == 0` (panel-failed) must precede the zero-findings check, and `LOOP_STATUS_OVERRIDE == main-agent-vote-required` must fire before any revise or convergence update. Check whether every edge case listed in the plan's 'Edge cases' section — zero-findings false positive on broken panel, main-agent-vote-required during a non-final round, revision-failed not treated as panel-failed — is correctly captured by the pseudocode's guard ordering as written. Verify that `DEGRADED_PANEL=1` is set BEFORE the convergence check inspects the streak, and that `convergence_streak` is reset to 0 for degraded rounds even when the threshold condition would simultaneously have been met. Identify any path through the pseudocode where two conditions could both be true and the wrong branch fires first. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"kv-surface-sync","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Checks that every KV key added to emit_loop_kvs is documented in the .md sibling and parsed in SKILL.md, with no orphaned, undeclared, or unhandled values across the three surfaces.","prompt_body":"The plan adds `IMPORTANT_ACCEPTED_COUNT`, `CONVERGENCE_STREAK`, `REASON`, and new `LOOP_STATUS` values to the emitted KV record, and `skills/design/SKILL.md` must parse and branch on each. Cross-check the three surfaces — the `emit_loop_kvs` extension in `plan-review-loop.sh`, the machine-output section in `plan-review-loop.md`, and the KV parsing and branch logic in `SKILL.md` — for any key that is emitted but not documented, documented but not parsed, or parsed but not branched on. Verify that the new `LOOP_STATUS` values (`converged`, `cap-hit`, `revision-failed`) are handled in every location that currently branches on `LOOP_STATUS` in SKILL.md, including the `STEP3_REVIEW_CAP_REACHED` guard and the `panel-failed` short-circuit path. Confirm that the plan does not silently retire the old `complete` value from the single-pass backward-compat path without documenting the omission. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"allowlist-drift-contract","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Audits the dual-allowlist contract between the loop snapshot helper and design-log-publish.sh for inconsistencies, missing source-of-truth designation, and whether tests actually catch drift.","prompt_body":"The plan introduces two parallel allowlists that must stay synchronized: the snapshot helper's `round_artifact_included()` inside `plan-review-loop.sh` and `design_round_artifact_included()` inside `design-log-publish.sh`. Verify that the plan explicitly designates one as the source of truth and specifies who owns additions or removals — the plan states 'publish is the superset for back-compat' but does not describe an update procedure when the loop adds a new artifact type. Check whether `findings-classification.tsv` is intentionally excluded from the loop snapshot but included in publish for back-compat, and confirm this asymmetry is explicitly documented rather than a silent gap. Assess whether the integration test in `test-design-multi-round-integration.sh` is actually constructed to detect allowlist drift — a test that only verifies expected files are present will miss the case where an unexpected file is also staged without error. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
